1. What changed: In [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L1315), the fused direct-MoE non-resident path no longer uploads every routed expert. It now computes top-k selection before staging, then uploads only the selected experts’ `up_proj`/`down_proj` pairs and builds `FusedNvfp4WeightView` arrays just for those staged weights.

2. How selected-only upload works: After gate logits are produced, the non-resident path copies the single-token router logits to host, runs `SelectTopExperts`, and stages only those selected expert weights ([expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L1334)). For the compact staged-view arrays, `selected_indices` is remapped to `0..top_k-1`, so `RunFusedMoeDirectDecode` indexes the staged views correctly instead of expecting a full 128-expert table ([expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L1416)).

3. Compile status: `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend -j4 2>&1 | tail -5` passed.

4. Any concerns: I only verified compilation. I did not rerun correctness or benchmark/staging-counter checks, so the remaining risk is runtime behavior on the non-resident layers. This path now pays a small per-token D2H copy for router logits, but it removes the much larger all-128-expert upload that was causing the VRAM failure.

